                <pb facs="0280" n="174" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg174"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Wilson to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <hi rendition="#italic"><date
                                calendar="gregorian" when="1906-03-28">March 28,
                        1906</date></hi>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Wilson reports that, under the department’s telegraphic instructions
                    received February 23 and March 25, he has been strongly urging the Government of
                    Japan to give real effect to their avowed open-door policy in Manchuria and says
                    that he hopes to report soon a definite answer to his notes. Representations are
                    also being made by the British Government.)</p>
            </div>
